      "id": 4,
      "text": "Default risk decreases with annual income and the length of the credit history, but increases with the debt-to-income ratio."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The number of recent inquiries, age, months at the current address, and number of dependents hardly matter for the model's predictions."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Credit utilization does not interact with income, debt-to-income ratio, credit history length, or the number of delinquencies."
    }
  ]
}

